## Finding

The [original incident](/kb/incidents/4471) called this one known issue with one fix.
Its rendered cause table contradicts that summary: the shared parser and the booking-form
hint fail in different ways. They need separate tickets and separate verification.

<Callout>
This review covers the export dated 2026-10-04, not the desk's current queue.
The review date records when the evidence was checked; it does not make that evidence live.
The tables recompute from the bundled data. New reports require a fresh export and rebuild.
</Callout>

<IncidentReview />

## Engineering disposition reported after the export

The [challenge page](https://hq.mega.dev/challenges/what-it-shows) subsequently reports
that ticket #4471 closed on 2026-10-05:

- **Parser: fixed**, with the message `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.
  [Our parser ticket](https://github.com/3750/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1)
  is closed as completed on that reported disposition.
- **Hint: won't fix**, because booking-v3 was retired.
  [Our hint ticket](https://github.com/3750/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2)
  is closed as not planned, not described as a code fix.

These are engineering's reported outcomes, not product-level tests performed in this review.
The counts above remain the historical export coverage. Closing the parser ticket does not
establish a diagnosis or fix for the unresolved body-level exceptions.

## Different failures, different fixes

**Shared parser:** Harbour Dental's app report `R-41200` describes 7 April becoming 4 July.
For a day-first tenant, the shared parser wrongly reads input month-first.
Use tenant-aware parsing, reject invalid dates, and round-trip the user's intended calendar date
through storage and invite creation. Verify app, email, and booking-v2 form paths.

**booking-v3 hint:** `R-41230` from Copper Studio's form is assigned to the hint problem,
despite its parser intake tag. The field prints `MM/DD/YYYY`, so people follow that format;
the form then interprets their input in the tenant's day-first order.
Make the displayed hint and accepted input agree. Verify Alder Physio, Copper Studio,
and Pale Harbour forms, plus app/email paths that still use the shared parser.
Changing only the shared parser does not correct the misleading field hint.

## Triage by evidence, not by subject

The explorer below runs the existing tenant, locale, form, and channel logic.
Its initial reports have matching subjects but different assigned causes.
Conversely, an app report and an email report can share a cause despite different subjects.
Unknown tenants and contradictory bodies remain unconfirmed; do not force them into either bucket.

<DedupeExplorer />

The immutable [accepted decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) records the old
subject-only rule. [Proposed successor 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-evidence-before-merge)
explains the replacement and its limits. This review does not claim the desk has approved it.

